1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Serialize the launch-claim mutation under the store write lock[bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]launch_claim_lock[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch_claim_lock: hold one bead_store_write_lock span across the runner[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch-claim mutation and its SDD commit in claim_bead_for_agent_launch,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]matching the sase-9r.1 contract already enforced on the wait-claim and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release paths.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Always commit retained claims and make release outcomes [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]tri-state[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]claim_persistence[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]claim_persistence: commit and publish a wait claim that is held but [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]still uncommitted after a retry, return distinct released/no-op/error [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]outcomes from claim release so shutdown can clear markers on no-ops, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]guard home-mode and in-tree claim publication, and enforce the push [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path's never-raises contract.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile claim residue and surface stuck beads in doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]residue_diagnostics[dim] · [dim][/dim]after claim_persistence[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]residue_diagnostics: give the bead_claim_checks chop a terminal [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tombstone for dead-owner records so it regains its zero-read steady [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state, and add report-only doctor advisories for dead-owner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]claimed/in_progress beads and dangling dependency edges.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Git probe failures must never read as clean[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]probe_fail_closed[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]probe_fail_closed: make bead_state_is_clean fail closed on probe errors,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]treat unexpected `git diff --cached` exit codes as errors in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit_sdd_files, and include unmerged_error in repository blockers and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollback-mismatch verification, finishing the sase-9r.3 sweep.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Managed sync worker cooldown, environment, redaction, and log [bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]fixes[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sync_worker_hygiene[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync_worker_hygiene: clear the failed-integration cooldown marker on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every successful integration path, stop mutating os.environ in-process, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]redact credentials in sync worker git errors via the shared formatter, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]give detached sync logs a unique collision-free writer, and drop the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]worker's redundant freshness marking.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fit the bead_store_refresh chop inside its own time budget[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]refresh_chop_budget[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh_chop_budget: bound the per-project lock wait of the chop's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocking refresh below the chop timeout, and persist backoff state so a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]timeout kill does not erase it; scoped to compose with the separately [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planned sase-9u refresh_cooldown phase.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Restore the bead work CLI confirmation, JSON, and reporting [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]contracts[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]bead_work_cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead_work_cli: honor --yes/--yes-to-all on epic resume instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hardcoding force-approval, restore the epic-launch task origin, emit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]JSON envelopes on every bead-id error path, report only real phases as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]phase beads, diagnose plan-file-only flags on bead-id targets, correct [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]misleading error/hint texts, and serialize bead-id launches under the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic launch lock.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Move legacy epic-approval preflight off the ACE event loop[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui_epic_approval_offload[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui_epic_approval_offload: run the legacy plan-approval modal's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic-launch preflight and submission through the tracked-task pattern [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the modern gate path already uses, so store materialization and lock [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]waits never block the Textual event loop.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make every sase-core bead mutation atomic against concurrent [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]writers[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_mutation_atomicity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\